WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.501
-We ran into each other
a few months ago

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.801
-Oh, yeah.
-...at a restaurant in L.A.

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:05.868
-Do you remember that?
-Of course I remember that.

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:06.634
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah. I didn't know.

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:08.300
-Yeah.
-I saw you.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.434
-I saw you eating.
You were with your girlfriend

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:11.367
and I thought it'd be funny.

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:13.000
I sent you over...
-An olive.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.667
-...one olive.
-One olive.

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:18.901
-I go, split it, eat it
yourself, whatever you want.

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:20.467
I don't want to tell you how
to eat your olive, yeah.

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:22.567
-Yeah, and then what did we do?
We sent you something.

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:23.968
-No, I'll tell you exactly
what you did.

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:25.767
You had the whole restaurant

00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:27.501
come over and sing me
happy birthday.

00:00:27.501 --> 00:00:29.000
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Oh, yes.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.334
-And it's not my birthday.

00:00:30.334 --> 00:00:32.067
-Yes.
-It was not my birthday at all.

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:34.000
[ Cheering and applause ]
I blew out the candle.

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.167
I blew out the candle.

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:40.501
It was not my birthday at all.
-It was not your birthday.

00:00:40.501 --> 00:00:43.100
-It was not my birthday,
but that really made me laugh.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.234
[ Cheering ]
That was good. But then

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:47.334
here's the best move.

00:00:47.334 --> 00:00:49.000
You were leaving.
-Yes.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.767
-There was a great guy
who plays music, guitar,

00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:53.734
at the -- at the Polo.

00:00:53.734 --> 00:00:55.133
-At the restaurant.
-At the restaurant.

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:57.400
[ Laughter ]
-We won't say where it is.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.367
We don't want to give it away.
At the restaurant.

00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:02.634
And so he starts singing
"Hey Jude,"

00:01:02.634 --> 00:01:04.901
and so I jumped up
to sing with him.

00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:08.534
-You did.
-And I thought you were gone.

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:10.200
-Well, no, we were still eating

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.200
and you were still singing
"Hey Jude."

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.801
[ Laughter ]
And then they do that whole

00:01:14.801 --> 00:01:16.767
end part, you know,
where it's just ♪ Ya ♪

00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:19.200
-♪ Na, na, na, na, na ♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.200
-And you just kept going.
It was amazing.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:24.834
I mean, really.

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:27.167
It was high, low.
-I was harmonizing with myself.

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:29.267
-You were harmonizing.

00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:31.300
-But then you --
Were you just leaving?

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.934
-Yeah, we were just leaving
and then, you know --

00:01:33.934 --> 00:01:36.534
-I grabbed you.
-Your energy, the whole

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:39.200
audience, the audience --
the restaurant was into it

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:42.534
and so, it was just like, let's
all sing, and we all started --

00:01:42.534 --> 00:01:44.767
-So we sang "Hey Jude" together.

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:46.167
Yeah, it was fantastic.

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:48.667
You have a great reputation
by the way, in Hollywood

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:51.267
of being a very nice guy,
and I will say,

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:54.133
you always have been nice.
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:54.133 --> 00:01:55.868
Always have been a cool guy
with me.

00:01:55.868 --> 00:01:58.834
-Fix my shirt.
Fix my tie.

00:01:58.834 --> 00:02:00.734
-Yeah.
You've always been great to me.

00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:03.367
But I saw this photo
that just --

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:05.467
everyone was talking about it
on the Internet.

00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:06.968
You crashed someone's wedding
in London.

00:02:06.968 --> 00:02:08.801
-I didn't crash their wedding.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.801 --> 00:02:10.601
-Well, it looks like
you weren't invited.

00:02:10.601 --> 00:02:13.000
I don't know.
-I sort of look like that.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.133
-I don't know if you crashed it,
but you definitely weren't--

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:18.701
-I was invited to meet some
folks and take a photo.

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:20.701
-Oh, sorry.
So you heard that people

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:21.667
were getting married
or something?

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:23.067
-No. It was outside

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:25.200
and there was another part
of the hotel

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.033
and it was outside of London
and they were having a wedding

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:31.000
and then the groom came by
and he was like, "Hi,"

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.334
and I was like, "Hi!"

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:34.000
And then he was like,
"Do you want to take a picture

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.300
with everybody?" And I said,
"Yeah, sure, let's do it,"

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.701
and meet some folks and then we
went in there and I said hi

00:02:38.701 --> 00:02:42.501
and hi and hi and then we took
some photographs and that's one

00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:44.234
of the photographs.
-It made their night.

00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:46.567
-One of these things does not
belong and it was me.

00:02:46.567 --> 00:02:48.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.167
-I would've sang "Hey Jude" with
them, if they asked me, yeah.

00:02:50.167 --> 00:02:52.167
[ Laughter ]
-It was really lovely.
It was cool.

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:53.534
-It's cool that you
do that stuff.
-Nice fun.

00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:55.601
Also, it's also cool that you do
this stuff, too.

00:02:55.601 --> 00:02:58.367
Can we talk about "Brzrkr"?
-Oh, you have "Brzrkr."

00:02:58.367 --> 00:03:01.501
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Oh, yeah, I have "Brzrkr."

00:03:01.501 --> 00:03:03.834
-It's a comic book.
-This is unbelievable.

00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:06.501
Now, this is just an idea
that you had and you go,

00:03:06.501 --> 00:03:08.834
"I'm just going to make this."

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:10.767
-Yeah, I cowrote it
with Matt Kindt

00:03:10.767 --> 00:03:13.701
and amazing illustrator
Ron Garney.

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:16.334
Issue 12.
It's a 12-issue limited series.

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:18.400
The last one came out yesterday.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.033
-Yeah.
Do you know the first --

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:21.801
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:26.734
-The first issue sold
over 650,000 copies, making it

00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:30.133
the highest selling indie comic
of the 21st century.

00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:32.200
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Wow. Thanks.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.968
Thanks, universe.
-Wow!

00:03:33.968 --> 00:03:36.234
-Thanks, everybody.
No, it's cool.

00:03:36.234 --> 00:03:38.000
I love comic books,
and having the chance

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.067
to do something like that
was really,

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:41.334
really special.
-How did you end up coming up

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:44.234
with the storyline
and everything?

00:03:44.234 --> 00:03:45.968
-Where do ideas come from?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.968 --> 00:03:48.434
-I know, yeah,
that's a very deep question.

00:03:48.434 --> 00:03:51.467
-Where do they --
it came to me -- What about

00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:53.567
a character that could punch
people through the chest?

00:03:53.567 --> 00:03:55.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.567
And then, like, what if they
were half God, half immortal?

00:03:58.567 --> 00:04:03.267
And then what if they were alive
for 80,000 years?

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:06.334
Then what would society do
with that

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:08.200
but then he's cursed
with violence.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.334
-He doesn't want to be violent.
-He doesn't want to be violent.

00:04:10.334 --> 00:04:12.400
-No, but it's in his blood.
-He can't die.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.968
Then he doesn't know
who his father is.

00:04:14.968 --> 00:04:17.234
-Are you kidding me?
-There's this tribe that like

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:19.734
asks the gods for a weapon
because they're being like

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:22.367
ambushed and exploited
every season.

00:04:22.367 --> 00:04:24.868
And then they get this kid --
-When are we seeing this movie?!

00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:26.467
[ Cheering ]
I want to see this! Come on!

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:29.567
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:29.567 --> 00:04:31.033
-Oh, and then he's like
being used

00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:33.367
by the United States government.
They're trying to like figure

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:35.033
him out, how does he tick.
-Yeah, of course the government

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:36.934
gets involved, yes!
-Of course. Yes!

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:38.467
-Black ops.
-But what would you do

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:39.667
with this idea, Keanu Reeves,

00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:41.501
if you couldn't have
this outlet?

00:04:41.501 --> 00:04:43.000
Would this just live
in your brain?

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:46.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.934 --> 00:04:48.667
I don't know. You did it.
-Yeah, I don't know.

00:04:48.667 --> 00:04:50.133
-You got it out.
-I don't know.

00:04:50.133 --> 00:04:52.801
I mean, it's like
the creative act

00:04:52.801 --> 00:04:55.434
is something special.
-It is, yeah.

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:57.000
-And it's storytelling.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:00.434
And what would I do
if I couldn't do that?

00:05:00.434 --> 00:05:03.100
I'd probably be on the street,
just babbling.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:05.434
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:05.434 --> 00:05:08.200
Would you make this
into a movie?

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.534
-Yeah, that'd be fun.

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:11.767
-Yeah.
Would you direct it?

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:14.534
-Mm. I don't know.
I don't know.

00:05:14.534 --> 00:05:17.868
We tried to shop it around
and then Netflix said,

00:05:17.868 --> 00:05:19.067
"Hey, do you want to make it
with us?"

00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:20.567
And I was like, "Sure."

00:05:20.567 --> 00:05:22.667
And then so we're going to try
and make that happen.

00:05:22.667 --> 00:05:24.167
-Whoa!
-Yeah.

00:05:24.167 --> 00:05:26.934
[ Cheering and applause ]
I love it.

00:05:26.934 --> 00:05:29.934
We have to talk
about "John Wick: Chapter 4."

00:05:29.934 --> 00:05:31.667
Buddy, you did it again.

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:33.100
It's unbelievable!

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:36.434
It's -- This one --
This one's the best.

00:05:36.434 --> 00:05:38.200
-What?
-This one is the best one.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:39.667
Yes!
-The best? What?

00:05:39.667 --> 00:05:41.434
-Plug your ears because I know
they're all your babies.

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:43.167
But I like this one.
-What? That's awesome.

00:05:43.167 --> 00:05:44.667
-The first one was like,
"Holy moly."

00:05:44.667 --> 00:05:46.033
-I know,
"What the heck is that?"

00:05:46.033 --> 00:05:48.467
-I loved it. I didn't know
the first one was even out.

00:05:48.467 --> 00:05:50.133
I don't know how I even saw
the first one.

00:05:50.133 --> 00:05:52.267
And I go, "Oh, my gosh." I think
I was in a hotel somewhere.

00:05:52.267 --> 00:05:54.300
I go, "This movie's phenomenal."
-That's kind.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:56.267
-I call my wife, I go, "You've
got to watch 'John Wick,' man."

00:05:56.267 --> 00:05:58.901
This is like I'm in all the way,
man, and we love you,

00:05:58.901 --> 00:06:00.267
and the whole Fallons love Keanu

00:06:00.267 --> 00:06:01.701
at the house, yeah.
-Oh, thanks, Jimmy.

00:06:01.701 --> 00:06:04.834
Well, you celebrate my birthday
when it's not my birthday.

00:06:04.834 --> 00:06:06.167
[ Laughter ]
It's great.

00:06:06.167 --> 00:06:09.067
This one has got it all.
It looks gorgeous.

00:06:09.067 --> 00:06:11.367
-Yeah, it's beautiful.
-It's a work of art.

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:14.400
The action starts maybe
five seconds into it

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:17.033
[ Laughter ]
and doesn't stop until you leave
the theater.

00:06:17.033 --> 00:06:18.234
-Yeah, there's a lot of action.

00:06:18.234 --> 00:06:20.534
-You're on a horse at one point.

00:06:20.534 --> 00:06:21.868
-Yeah.
-Shooting people.

00:06:21.868 --> 00:06:24.033
-Well, you know, I'm -- Yeah.

00:06:24.033 --> 00:06:25.033
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:25.033 --> 00:06:26.567
There's nunchucks.

00:06:26.567 --> 00:06:27.868
-Yes, there are.
-Yeah.

00:06:27.868 --> 00:06:29.501
There's throwing stars.

00:06:29.501 --> 00:06:30.934
-Yeah.
-There's --

00:06:30.934 --> 00:06:33.000
-Driving.
-By the way.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.701
-Crazy driving.
-Driving scenes with no doors.

00:06:34.701 --> 00:06:36.701
-Yeah, yeah.
-No windows maybe at one point.

00:06:36.701 --> 00:06:39.133
-They got blown out, too.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.133 --> 00:06:42.467
-There's just a steering wheel
and wheels, that's all it is.

00:06:42.467 --> 00:06:43.634
It's like a go-cart,
by the end of it.

00:06:43.634 --> 00:06:45.901
-No, that's an American
muscle car.

00:06:45.901 --> 00:06:48.934
I'm like throwing 180s.
-Oh, my gosh!

00:06:48.934 --> 00:06:50.400
-Doing John Wick things.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:53.367
-I read somewhere there's
14 action sequences.

00:06:53.367 --> 00:06:54.501
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:06:54.501 --> 00:06:57.000
-And it's all choreographed
brilliantly.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.634
-Yeah, most of the time.

00:06:58.634 --> 00:06:59.834
[ Laughter ]

00:06:59.834 --> 00:07:01.734
I mean, it's always --
Well, I can't say

00:07:01.734 --> 00:07:03.534
it's always choreographed.
-Is there improvising ever?

00:07:03.534 --> 00:07:07.534
-Yeah, kind of, yeah.
-And does that end well?

00:07:07.534 --> 00:07:08.934
No?
-Yes.

00:07:08.934 --> 00:07:11.868
No humans were harmed
in the making of this film.

00:07:11.868 --> 00:07:14.801
[ Laughter ]
-Thank you, yeah.
-No, I mean, there's a lot --

00:07:14.801 --> 00:07:17.300
the director,
visionary Chad Stahelski,

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:21.100
is very inventive
and he really wants to create

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:24.234
different kinds of environments

00:07:24.234 --> 00:07:28.267
or ways in the storytelling
for the action.

00:07:28.267 --> 00:07:30.667
-He's got to be a genius
because, I mean, this is

00:07:30.667 --> 00:07:32.567
the fourth one and you're still
reinventing new ways.

00:07:32.567 --> 00:07:34.400
I go,
"Oh, that shot is gorgeous!

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.868
How did you even come up
with that?"

00:07:35.868 --> 00:07:39.133
The cars on its side, the lights
hitting you at a certain thing.

00:07:39.133 --> 00:07:40.701
-Cinema.

00:07:40.767 --> 00:07:41.767
[ Laughter ]
Cinema.

00:07:41.834 --> 00:07:43.267
-It feels like cinema.
-Cinema.

00:07:43.267 --> 00:07:45.734
It feels like you're
watching -- Yes!

00:07:45.734 --> 00:07:46.467
-Cinema.

00:07:46.467 --> 00:07:48.701
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:50.901
-What can we say
about "John Wick" and this one

00:07:50.901 --> 00:07:53.868
that's not spoiling anything?
Or can I just -- Can we just --

00:07:53.868 --> 00:07:56.968
Like I know you want to get out.
Like always.

00:07:56.968 --> 00:07:58.767
You don't want to do this.
-I don't.

00:07:58.767 --> 00:08:00.567
I'm looking
for my personal freedom.

00:08:00.567 --> 00:08:01.801
-Yes!
-You know?

00:08:01.801 --> 00:08:03.467
It starts with trying to get
my ring back,

00:08:03.467 --> 00:08:05.534
but that doesn't work so well,
so then...

00:08:05.534 --> 00:08:07.033
-No.
-...I get a little angry.

00:08:07.033 --> 00:08:08.367
[ Laughter ]
But then --

00:08:08.367 --> 00:08:10.167
But I'm looking
for my personal freedom.

00:08:10.167 --> 00:08:12.033
There's a whole bunch
of new characters

00:08:12.033 --> 00:08:14.734
who are opening up the world
of the High Table.

00:08:14.734 --> 00:08:16.167
-Who plays Caine?

00:08:16.167 --> 00:08:18.100
-Caine is Donnie Yen.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.267
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:08:19.267 --> 00:08:21.133
He's a legend.

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:24.934
Hiroyuki Sanada. Rina Sawayama,
who was on your show.

00:08:24.934 --> 00:08:27.868
-Rina Sawayama is fantastic.
She was on last night.

00:08:27.868 --> 00:08:30.300
-She's awesome.
-It's a crusher cast.

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:33.501
-Shamier Anderson.
So we have The Tracker.

00:08:33.501 --> 00:08:36.133
We have Caine, we have Shimazu,

00:08:36.133 --> 00:08:37.667
so all of these
different characters.

00:08:37.667 --> 00:08:40.534
It's friendship, brotherhood,
father, daughter,

00:08:40.534 --> 00:08:43.834
the choices that you make,
rules and consequences,

00:08:43.834 --> 00:08:45.534
who are you, man?

00:08:45.534 --> 00:08:47.100
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Wow! Come on!

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:48.334
-And here's how it's gonna work.

00:08:48.334 --> 00:08:50.968
I'll be asking both of you
animal trivia questions.

00:08:50.968 --> 00:08:52.100
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:54.200
And if you answer correctly,

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:56.367
